<title>USA: Trustmark Corp Q1 $0.49 vs $0.44.</title>
<headline>Trustmark Corp Q1 $0.49 vs $0.44.</headline>
<dateline>JACKSON, Miss. 1997-04-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>First Qtr 1997	First Qtr 1996(a)</p>
<p> Total Assets (billion)	   $5.377		     $5.195</p>
<p>Stockholders' Equity (million)</p>
<p>					 547.742		    485.883</p>
<p> Net Income (million)	     17.675		     15.369</p>
<p> Net Income/share			.49			  .44</p>
<p>NOTE: (a) Prior years' financial statements were not restated as the changes would have been immaterial.</p>
<p>During the first quarter of 1997, Trustmark Corp completed its merger with First Corinth Corporation (FCC) and its subsidiary, National Bank of Commerce (NBC). The corporation issued approximately 1.5 million shares of common stock in the merger which was accounted for as a pooling of interests.  As a result of this transaction, the Corporation has restated its financial statements to include FCC and NBC as of Jan. 1, 1997.</p>
</text>
